---
layout: base.njk
title: Conditions — Toza
description: "Toza's prices and commercial terms on one printable page: the first step, protection tiers, Annual Care, urgent visits and payment."
permalink: false
---
{% set pr = facts.prices %}
<div class="wrap pt-8 pb-14 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-24 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">

  <aside class="cond-toc hidden lg:block lg:col-span-3 print:hidden" aria-label="Sections">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#prices">Prices</a></li>
      <li><a href="#first-step">The first step</a></li>
      <li><a href="#thirty-day">The 30-day rule</a></li>
      <li><a href="#tier-choice">When a household needs more</a></li>
      <li><a href="#allowances">Allowances in every tier</a></li>
      <li><a href="#question-line">The {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line</a></li>
      <li><a href="#annual-care">Annual Care</a></li>
      <li><a href="#urgent">Urgent visits</a></li>
      <li><a href="#payment">Payment before work</a></li>
    </ol>
  </aside>

  <article class="cond lg:col-span-9" aria-labelledby="h1">
    <header>
      <img class="print-only-logo" src="/assets/brand/toza-logo-ink.svg" alt="" width="421" height="154">
      <h1 id="h1" class="display text-[2.625rem] sm:text-6xl lg:text-[4.25rem] !text-ink">Prices and conditions.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 lg:mt-8 text-lg lg:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-[38rem] text-text">Every engagement is carried out by Dr. Lior Tabansky in person, at your home or office, with you present and in control of your credentials. Each price is fixed and agreed in writing before work begins.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-muted">
        <span>Terms as of 16 October 2026.</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost print:hidden" onclick="window.print()">{{ t.ui.print }}</button>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section id="prices" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="prices-h">
      <h2 id="prices-h" class="cond-h">Prices</h2>
      <table class="cond-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Prices by service</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">For</th><th scope="col">Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Private Exposure Assessment (first step)</th><td>Everyone starts here</td><td>{{ pr.assessment | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Personal Shield</th><td>One person</td><td>{{ pr.personalShield | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Personal Shield for Two</th><td>You and one other person</td><td>{{ pr.shieldForTwo | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Inner Circle</th><td>A household of up to four</td><td>{{ pr.innerCircle | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Larger households, several residences or household staff</th><td>One fixed price, set after the first step</td><td>from {{ pr.largerFrom | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Annual Care, one person</th><td>Past clients</td><td>{{ pr.annualCareOne | ils }} a year</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Annual Care for two</th><td>Past clients</td><td>{{ pr.annualCareTwo | ils }} a year</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Annual Care, household of up to four</th><td>Past clients</td><td>{{ pr.annualCareHousehold | ils }} a year</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Urgent visit surcharge</th><td>Added to the agreed service price</td><td>{{ pr.urgentSurcharge | ils }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Urgent visit surcharge, weekend or holiday</th><td>Replaces the ordinary surcharge</td><td>{{ pr.urgentSurchargeWeekend | ils }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mt-5">All prices include VAT.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="first-step" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="first-h">
      <h2 id="first-h" class="cond-h">The first step: Private Exposure Assessment</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>Covers {{ facts.assessmentScope }}, with the relevant identities, accounts, apps, permissions, recovery routes and shared services.</li>
        <li>Half a day in person, typically four hours. The visit completes the agreed intake, access mapping, diagnosis and approved urgent first aid, including removing a malicious app or profile where that can be done safely.</li>
        <li>Four hours is a guide; the visit completes its agreed scope.</li>
        <li>You receive a written exposure summary of what was reviewed, found and changed, what remains and the next steps, whether or not you continue.</li>
        <li>For Personal Shield for Two and Inner Circle, the first step covers the first person's devices. The other people are reviewed within the tier.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="thirty-day" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="thirty-h">
      <h2 id="thirty-h" class="cond-h">The 30-day rule</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>The {{ pr.assessment | ils }} counts in full toward a tier whose work begins within {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days of completion of the first step. You then pay the balance.</li>
        <li>Balances: Personal Shield {{ pr.balanceShield | ils }} · Personal Shield for Two {{ pr.balanceTwo | ils }} · Inner Circle {{ pr.balanceInnerCircle | ils }}.</li>
        <li>After day {{ facts.credit.windowDays }}, the tier is charged at its full price.</li>
        <li>Moving up a tier: if the first step shows the next tier is needed, you pay that tier's price less the {{ pr.assessment | ils }} already paid, within the same {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days.</li>
        <li>The first step counts once per engagement, also for a group.</li>
        <li>Larger households: the fixed price is set in writing after the first step, from {{ pr.largerFrom | ils }}, and the {{ pr.assessment | ils }} counts toward it on the same {{ facts.credit.windowDays }}-day terms.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="tier-choice" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="choice-h">
      <h2 id="choice-h" class="cond-h">When a household needs more</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>If the first step shows more than a tier includes, such as more people or devices, a second home, staff or company devices, Dr. Tabansky proposes the next tier, with its full allowance, before any work begins.</li>
        <li>Beyond Inner Circle, he sets one fixed price in writing.</li>
        <li>Each tier has one fixed price for everything within its allowance.</li>
        <li>Agreed additions are separate, and any added scope or price is agreed in writing before that work begins.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="allowances" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="allow-h">
      <h2 id="allow-h" class="cond-h">Allowances in every tier</h2>
      {% set dpp = facts.devicesPerPerson %}
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>Everyday devices (phone, computer, tablet or second phone): up to {{ dpp | numword }} per person, shared within the tier. Personal Shield {{ dpp | numword }}, Personal Shield for Two {{ (dpp * 2) | numword }}, Inner Circle {{ (dpp * 4) | numword }}.</li>
        <li>Security keys, supplied, configured and tested: Personal Shield {{ facts.securityKeys.personalShield | numword }}, Personal Shield for Two {{ facts.securityKeys.shieldForTwo | numword }}, Inner Circle {{ facts.securityKeys.innerCircle | numword }}.</li>
        <li>One home network and router, in addition to the devices. The work covers accessible settings and authorized administration. Replacement hardware, further connected devices and additional locations are quoted separately.</li>
        <li>Essential migration covers identity, recovery routes and critical-service access where needed. Historical archives and bulk data migration are scoped separately.</li>
        <li>A follow-up visit after about four weeks.</li>
        <li>Questions answered by WhatsApp or Signal for {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days (see <a class="link" href="#question-line">the {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line</a>).</li>
        <li>Coordination with your lawyer or family office, if you authorize it.</li>
        <li>A private dated record for each person; home-network work is recorded separately.</li>
        <li>Inner Circle adds a review visit at twelve months.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="question-line" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="qline-h">
      <h2 id="qline-h" class="cond-h">The {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>Questions answered by WhatsApp or Signal within one working day, for {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days from completion of the tier's work.</li>
        <li>For questions and guidance about the work done. New work is agreed and priced separately; urgent needs go through an urgent visit.</li>
        <li>After the {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days, the line can continue through Annual Care.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="annual-care" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="care-h">
      <h2 id="care-h" class="cond-h">Annual Care</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>For past clients, after the {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line. Twelve months of:
          <ul class="terms-sub">
            <li>Questions answered by WhatsApp or Signal within one working day, as before</li>
            <li>A check visit in person: devices, accounts, recovery settings and keys re-checked, and your dated record updated</li>
            <li>A new or replaced phone or computer set up the same way</li>
            <li>A replacement security key if one is lost or broken</li>
            <li>First available appointments</li>
            <li>Coordination with your lawyer or family office, if you authorize it</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>{{ pr.annualCareOne | ils }} a year for one person, {{ pr.annualCareTwo | ils }} for two, {{ pr.annualCareHousehold | ils }} for a household of up to four. Paid yearly in advance.</li>
        <li>The term starts the day the {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line ends.</li>
        <li>For a household of up to four, Annual Care covers up to two new or replaced devices and up to two replacement keys. For Inner Circle, the first Care term moves the check visit to about month six; the twelve-month review stays.</li>
        <li>Further keys and any replacement router are charged at cost. Added devices are scoped separately.</li>
        <li>Joining: within {{ facts.annualCare.joinWindowMonths | numword }} months of the question line ending. After that, we start again with a first step ({{ pr.assessment | ils }}), which counts in full toward Annual Care within {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days.</li>
        <li>Renewal: at the published price at the time. The invoice is sent 30 days before the term ends, and the line stays open for 14 days while it is settled.</li>
        <li>Scoped and priced separately: new people; a new or second home; company devices or staff; devices beyond the original allowance; any incident, such as a suspected compromise; urgent visits, on the <a class="link" href="#urgent">urgent terms</a> below.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="urgent" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="urgent-h">
      <h2 id="urgent-h" class="cond-h">Urgent visits</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>Availability is confirmed before you pay.</li>
        <li>For an accepted urgent booking, arrival is within four hours of both Toza's acceptance and receipt of payment. The clock starts when both conditions are met.</li>
        <li>The four hours are an arrival commitment; the visit then runs its agreed course.</li>
        <li>Surcharge {{ pr.urgentSurcharge | ils }}, added to the agreed base service price. At weekends or holidays the surcharge is {{ pr.urgentSurchargeWeekend | ils }}, replacing the ordinary surcharge. Other charges apply only if separately agreed.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="payment" class="cond-s" aria-labelledby="pay-h">
      <h2 id="pay-h" class="cond-h">Payment before work</h2>
      <ol class="terms">
        <li>Every paid service follows three steps: a written scope and price (the work, inclusions, exclusions, price, agreed additions and payment terms); your explicit acceptance; receipt of payment. The work is then scheduled.</li>
        <li>This applies to the first step, each tier or its balance, Annual Care and any agreed addition.</li>
        <li>The first conversation is free and commits you to nothing.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <footer class="cond-foot print:hidden">
      <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Questions about these terms?</p>
      <p class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-1">
        <a class="link" href="{{ contact.whatsapp.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t.buttons.whatsapp }}</a>
        <a class="link" href="{{ contact.signal.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t.buttons.signal }}</a>
        <a class="link" href="{{ contact.callback.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t.buttons.callback }}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="link" href="/en/faq/">Privacy, boundaries and other questions: FAQ <span class="flip" aria-hidden="true">{{ t.ui.arrow }}</span></a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</div>
